{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.instHabiroRigidityComplexUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.instHabiroRigidityComplexUnit","kind":"instance","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity.lean#L71-L80","doc":"**The class is non-vacuous (shape-witness).** `H = ℂ`, one root of unity (`RootIndex = Unit`),\n`evalRoot` the identity and `evalQ0 = Re`: the identity evaluation is genuinely injective, so\n`root_injective` holds with real content. This witnesses the rigidity shape is inhabited by an\nhonestly-injective evaluation; it does **not** model the actual `z`-Habiro ring (the open object). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.q0_value_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.q0_value_unique","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity.lean#L59-L69","doc":"**Rigidity ⇒ no fit — conditional uniqueness, derived sorry-free from the class.** If two Habiro\nelements `w w'` have the **same root-of-unity values** (both realize the colored-WRT fibre data\n`bwS0Concrete`), then they have the **same archimedean `q₀` value** `τ_∞`. The fibre data forces the\nobservable value; it cannot be tuned. Fully verified **modulo the class instance** — the instance\nfor the actual `z`-Habiro ring (Habiro's theorem) is the open input, not proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity.root_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity.root_injective","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity.lean#L57-L57","doc":"**Content — Habiro injectivity (hypothesis).** A Habiro element is determined by its\nroot-of-unity values: if `a` and `b` agree at every root of unity, then `a = b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity.evalQ0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity.evalQ0","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Archimedean `q₀`-value (`τ_∞` evaluation) of a Habiro element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity.evalRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity.evalRoot","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Root-of-unity evaluation: value of a Habiro element at the root of unity indexed by `ζ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HabiroRigidity","kind":"class","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity.lean#L44-L57","doc":"**Habiro rigidity (§3b class).** An abstract Habiro-like element type `H` equipped with a\nroot-of-unity evaluation `evalRoot ζ : H → ℂ` (value at each root of unity `ζ`, indexed by\n`RootIndex`) and an archimedean `q₀`-value `evalQ0 : H → ℝ` (the `τ_∞` evaluation post-fibre-functor).\nThe content is **`root_injective`**: an element of `H` is **determined by its root-of-unity values**\n— Habiro's injectivity miracle, carried here as the class **hypothesis** (not proved). Any instance\nsupplies this rigidity; the actual `z`-Habiro ring realizing it is the open object. ","signatureChunk":0}]}